  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">eDNA Expeditions II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">eDNA Expeditions II project, is a citizen science initiative funded by the Minderoo Foundation and coordinated by UNESCO-IOC through its Ocean Biodiversity Information System (OBIS). Building on a prior phase, the project aims to establish long-term, repeated environmental DNA (eDNA) sampling in UNESCO marine protected areas globally. It focuses on capacity development and outreach for local communities and scientists, improving data processing and analysis workflows, and creating an accessible eDNA data dashboard within OBIS to enhance marine biodiversity knowledge and support data-driven conservation decisions.</narrative>
  </description>
